M methylammonium iodide and $0.8\mathrm{~M~}$ lead chloride in N, N-dimethylformamide (DMF). The spin-coated perovskite thin film was then dried at $65~^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ for $15~\mathrm{min}$ and annealed at $105\mathrm{~}^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ for $45\ \mathrm{min}$ until the color turned to dark brown. To prepare the 2,2’,7,7’-tetrakis(N,N-di-p-methoxyphenylamine)-9,9-spirobifluorene (spiro-MeOTAD) solution, $29\mathrm{\textmul}$ of 4-tert-butyl pyridine and $18~\upmu\mathrm{l}$ of lithium bis(trifluoromethanesulfonyl)imide (Li-TFSI) solution ( $520~\mathrm{\mg}$ Li-TFSI in $1\mathrm{\ml}$ acetonitride, Sigma-Aldrich, $99.8\%$ ) was added into $953~\mathrm{\textmul}$ of chlorobenzene dissolved with $80~\mathrm{mg}$ spiro-MeOTAD powder. The solution was then spin coated on the perovskite layer at 4500 rpm for 30s. The prepared FTO/c-TiO2/CH3NH3PbI3- $\mathrm{_{x}C l_{x}},$ spiro-MeDTAD films were annealed in oxygen to enhance the cell performance. Finally, MoO3/Au/MoO3 electrodes ( $15\ \mathrm{nm}/\ 12\ \mathrm{nm}/\ 20$ nm) were evaporated onto the devices, through which the device active area was defined as $0.06~\mathrm{cm}^{2}$ . The solar source was provided by the Newport solar simulator (ORIEL Sol3ATM) and the electrical measurement was performed by B1500A semiconductor analyzer. The absorption spectra of perovskite film on quartz were examined using a UV-2550 Shimadzu UV-Vis spectrophotometer. X-ray diffraction (XRD) patterns of the perovskite film was determined by a Rigaku SmartLab X-ray diffractometer with a 2θ range from $10^{\circ}$ to $70^{\circ}$ in a step of $0.01^{\circ}$ . Scanning electron microscopy (SEM) image was performed by Hitachi S-4800 field emission scanning electron microscope.
## Fabrication and Characterization of Electrochromic Supercapacitor. A 300
nm-thick $\mathrm{WO}_{3}$ thin film was thermally evaporated onto an FTO substrate as
## ACS Nano
supercapacitor electrode. The deposition was carried out with the background pressure of ${5\times10}^{-6}$ Torr and the chamber pressure during the deposition was maintained at $3{\times}10^{-5}$ Torr. The symmetric electrochromic supercapacitor was assembled by two identical $\mathrm{WO}_{3}$ electrodes coated with the mixture of polyvinyl alcohol (PVA) and 1M ${\mathrm{H}}_{2}{\mathrm{SO}}_{4}$ . Atomic force microscopy (AFM) image was examined by Bruker nanoscope 8. The electrochemical performances were characterized by electrochemical working station (CHI 660e, Shanghai Chenhua).
Integrated Device Characterization. The photo-charging process was performed under AM 1.5 illumination and the supercapacitor was discharged through electrochemical workstation. The transmittance spectra were obtained by using the UV-2550 Shimadzu UV-Vis spectrophotometer.
